To find $\dfrac{dy}{dx}$, we will need to use the product rule twice!

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[u(x)\cdot v(x) \cdot w(x)\right]
\\\\
&=u'(x)\cdot \Bigl(v(x)\cdot w(x) \Bigr)+u(x)\cdot\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[v(x)\cdot w(x)\right]&\gray{\text{Product rule}}
\\\\
&=u'(x)\cdot \Bigl(v(x)\cdot w(x) \Bigr)+u(x)\cdot\Bigl(v'(x)\cdot w(x)+v(x)w'(x)\Bigr)&\gray{\text{Product rule}}
\\\\
&= u'(x)\cdot v(x) \cdot w(x) + u(x) \cdot v'(x) \cdot w(x) + u(x) \cdot v(x) \cdot w'(x)
\end{align}$
